<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Shape for the pause screen's picture.

     From M3 (m3-expressive, references/tokens.md): the corner scale's Extra large step is 28dp
     (CornerExtraLarge). All four corners, uniformly.

     My design decision (not in M3): the picture is the only rounded rectangle on the screen. The
     countdown next to it is a full circle, and that square-vs-circle contrast is the expressive
     gesture. Giving the picture asymmetric corners as well would be a second gesture on the same
     screen pulling the eye the other way, so it stays even. -->
<resources>
    <style name="PausePointImageShape" parent="">
        <item name="cornerFamily">rounded</item>
        <item name="cornerSize">28dp</item>
    </style>
</resources>
